<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Gehrig returns six weeks after the diagnosis, a week after his first full visit to the multidisciplinary ALS clinic, where he saw the physical, occupational and speech therapists, the dietitian, the respiratory therapist and the social worker. He has taken riluzole twice daily; he had mild nausea in the first week, which settled. The genetic panel found no disease-causing variant in SOD1, C9orf72, FUS, TARDBP or the other genes tested. His grip is weaker and he has tripped twice without falling; the clinic measured him for a left ankle-foot orthosis. He has decided to stop playing professionally and plans to say so publicly soon, and he is thinking about work he could do at a desk. He has been sleeping poorly and feels low at times but enjoys time with friends. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Riluzole</td><td>Twice daily; nausea in the first week, settled</td></tr><tr><td>Genetic testing</td><td>No disease-causing variant found</td></tr><tr><td>Function</td><td>Grip weaker; two trips without a fall; orthosis measured</td></tr><tr><td>Work</td><td>Decided to stop playing; considering desk work</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>Low at times; poor sleep</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

