<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, limb onset (G12.21)</content>. Slow progression: ALSFRS-R 40 (42 at diagnosis), FVC 4.31 L (84%), maximal inspiratory pressure -80 cmH2O, weight 88.4 kg (0.9% below diagnosis). ALT 38 and AST 33 U/L on riluzole. No SOD1 variant, so tofersen does not apply; no family history of ALS is known. The one-month liver test was missed and is recorded as a protocol deviation. [S]<list><item>Continue riluzole; ALT at two and three months.</item><item>Left ankle-foot orthosis and a cane for outdoors; home exercise plan; button hook and adapted cutlery.</item><item>High-calorie diet; gastrostomy explained early, while breathing is strong.</item><item>Voice banking introduced by the speech therapist.</item><item>Workplace accommodations and disability benefits with the social worker.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Coping with ALS and leaving professional play</content>. PHQ-9 8 (mild); no thoughts of self-harm. Grief at leaving the game; good supports. [S]<list><item>Sessions with the ALS clinic psychologist.</item><item>Sleep advice; review at each visit.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>ALSFRS-R</td><td>Every 2 to 3 months in the multidisciplinary ALS clinic</td><td>Completed today</td><td>40 of 48 (42 at diagnosis)</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Seated forced vital capacity</td><td>Every 2 to 3 months in the multidisciplinary ALS clinic</td><td>Completed today</td><td>4.31 L, 84% of predicted</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Maximal inspiratory pressure; supine capacity and overnight oximetry when values fall or symptoms appear</td><td>Every 2 to 3 months in the multidisciplinary ALS clinic</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Maximal inspiratory pressure -80 cmH2O; no orthopnea</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Noninvasive ventilation criteria (FVC below 50%, maximal inspiratory pressure weaker than -60 cmH2O, nocturnal desaturation, orthopnea)</td><td>Every 2 to 3 months in the multidisciplinary ALS clinic</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No criterion met</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight and BMI (gastrostomy discussion if weight falls 5 to 10% or swallowing is unsafe; place while FVC is above 50%)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>88.4 kg, 0.9% below diagnosis</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Speech and swallowing assessment</td><td>Every 2 to 3 months in the multidisciplinary ALS clinic</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Normal at the clinic speech assessment; voice banking introduced</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Depression (PHQ-9)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 8, mild</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Symptoms: cramps, spasticity, saliva, emotional lability, pain</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Night cramps, eased by stretching; no spasticity problems, drooling or emotional lability</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Mobility, falls, orthoses and equipment</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Foot drop; orthosis measured; cane advised</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>ALT on riluzole</td><td>Monthly for 3 months, then every 3 months</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Missed: no liver test was drawn at one month because no visit fell then. ALT 38 U/L today, at six weeks, is normal, so no harm resulted. Corrective action: two- and three-month tests booked with the ALS clinic laboratory</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Genetic testing (SOD1 result decides tofersen)</td><td>Offer at diagnosis to every person with ALS</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No disease-causing variant in SOD1, C9orf72, FUS, TARDBP or the other genes tested; tofersen not indicated</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Multidisciplinary ALS clinic</td><td>Every 2 to 3 months in the multidisciplinary ALS clinic</td><td>Completed today</td><td>First full clinic visit last week</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Work, disability benefits and social work</td><td>From diagnosis</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Stopping professional play; exploring desk work and benefits with the social worker</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Advance care planning</td><td>Early, then at each change</td><td>Due</td><td>Planned for the preventive visit, at his choice</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>A clear diagnosis, with mimics excluded, within four weeks. Outcome by 1939-05-18: Diagnosis made at two weeks on EMG, MRI and blood tests [S]</item><item>No falls, using an ankle-foot orthosis, a cane, and a safer home. In progress; target 1939-10-19 [S]</item><item>Weight held within 5% of the weight at diagnosis. In progress; target 1939-10-19 [S]</item><item>Breathing tracked every visit, with noninvasive ventilation started as soon as criteria are met. In progress; target 1939-10-19 [S]</item><item>Goals of care, a health care agent, and his wishes about ventilation and feeding recorded early and revisited. In progress; target 1939-09-21 [S]</item><item>Working in a role that suits him, with accommodations. In progress; target 1939-10-19 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Practice parameter update: the care of the patient with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis: drug, nutritional, and respiratory therapies (an evidence-based review) (2009); Practice parameter update: the care of the patient with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis: multidisciplinary care, symptom management, and cognitive/behavioral impairment (an evidence-based review) (2009); Evidence-based consensus guidelines for ALS genetic testing and counseling (2023); Trial of Antisense Oligonucleotide Tofersen for SOD1 ALS (2022)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Liver tests at two and three months. ALS clinic in about two months, with primary care the same week. Next scheduled visit 1939-08-24: three months after diagnosis: ALSFRS-R, breathing, weight, speech, mobility equipment, and work accommodations. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
